    <p><br></p>
    <h4 id=3D"Parent/Childfirmconfiguration(Firm360)-WhynotusethecurrentPar=
ent_ID?"><strong>Why not use the current Parent_ID?</strong></h4>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"504f944d-db5c-4bec-b107-51ef6f98f914">A system-genera=
ted ID such as this one is not advisable for client-facing API's.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <h4 id=3D"Parent/Childfirmconfiguration(Firm360)-What'snext?"><strong>W=
hat's next?</strong></h4>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"ebf99094-4c0b-4adb-a49d-510389df2585">We will share t=
he target date for this implementation on Firm360 in a few days. After that=
, we can discuss how soon you can start incorporating it into the Compass j=
ob. <span>=E2=80=8B</span><span>=E2=80=8B</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
    <h4 id=3D"Parent/Childfirmconfiguration(Firm360)-Firmsetuplifecycle">Fi=
rm setup lifecycle</h4>
    <ul>
     <li data-uuid=3D"62afebba-a453-40a0-9aa7-9b36fbe773ba">When a new firm=
 is created in Firm360, they are always associated to a parent firm, whethe=
r the parent firm is shared by other firms or not</li>
     <li data-uuid=3D"bffe824e-e05c-4c48-ab29-7f620f21233a">When there is a=
 merge, child firms will be grouped under the same parent firm&nbsp;</li>
    </ul>
    <p><br></p>
