 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p><strong>Inheritance properties</strong></p>
    <ul>
     <li>Have to do it case by case. For example, in firm digital packaging=
, a parent firm's selection may/may not be cascaded to the child firms.</li=
>
     <li>Permission / Resource visibility: Example - A parent firm user has=
 Trader role but the child firm does not have access to Trading module.&nbs=
p;</li>
    </ul>
    <p>.</p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
 <div class=3D"columnLayout single" data-layout=3D"single">
  <div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
   <div class=3D"innerCell">
    <p><strong>UI data aggregation - NOT to be centralized</strong></p>
    <ul>
     <li>When a parent firm user accesses a page or resource, whether only =
the data pertained to the selected child firm or data of all firms are depi=
cted would be prescribed by the respective product.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>.</p>
   </div>
  </div>
 </div>
